<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Identity security assessment: {{ alias }}</title>
<style>{{ base_css }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<div class="brandbar"><span class="mark">iA</span> IAMAI <span class="sub">&middot; identity posture assessment</span></div>
<h1>Identity security assessment</h1>
<p class="meta">Tenant: {{ alias }}. Generated {{ generated_at }}.
{% if collected_at %}Based on data collected {{ collected_at }}.{% endif %}</p>

{% for warning in data_warnings %}
<div class="banner"><strong>Some data is incomplete.</strong> {{ warning }}</div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>This report grades the tenant against the standard, a reference configuration
captured from a known good setup. Each area below is judged conservatively:
when the data is ambiguous, the grade goes down, never up.</p>

<div class="tiles">
{% for group in groups %}
  <div class="tile {{ group.status }}">
    <h3>{{ group.label }}</h3>
    <span class="status"><span class="icon">{{ group.statusIcon }}</span>{{ group.statusLabel }}</span>
    <div class="count">{{ group.met }} of {{ group.total }} control{{ 's' if group.total != 1 }} meet the standard</div>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<p class="totals">Across all {{ total_controls }} controls:
{% for grade in grade_order %}{{ grade }} {{ grade_counts[grade] }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.</p>

<dl class="legend">
{% for grade in grade_order %}
  <dt>{{ grade }}</dt><dd>{{ grade_meanings[grade] }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>

{% for group in groups %}
<h2>{{ group.label }}</h2>
{% for control in group.controls %}
<section class="control">
  <header>
    <h3>{{ control.intent or "This control matches the standard's configuration." }}</h3>
    <span class="grade {{ grade_status[control.grade] }}"><span class="dot"></span>{{ control.grade }}</span>
  </header>
  {% if control.rationale %}<p class="rationale">{{ control.rationale }}</p>{% endif %}
  <div class="detail">
    {% if control.coverageGaps %}
    <p><strong>What is not covered:</strong></p>
    <ul>{% for gap in control.coverageGaps[:8] %}<li>{{ gap }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% if control.coverageGaps | length > 8 %}
    <details>
      <summary>Show the remaining {{ control.coverageGaps | length - 8 }} of {{ control.coverageGaps | length }} gaps</summary>
      <ul>{% for gap in control.coverageGaps[8:] %}<li>{{ gap }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    </details>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if control.notes %}
    <ul>{% for note in control.notes[:8] %}<li>{{ note }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% if control.notes | length > 8 %}
    <details>
      <summary>Show the remaining {{ control.notes | length - 8 }} of {{ control.notes | length }} notes</summary>
      <ul>{% for note in control.notes[8:] %}<li>{{ note }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    </details>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if control.matchedPolicies %}
    <p>Evidence: {% for policy in control.matchedPolicies %}{{ policy.displayName }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p>Accounts this applies to: {{ control.affected.count }}{% if control.affected.sampleUPNs %}
    (for example {% for upn in control.affected.sampleUPNs %}{{ upn }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}){% endif %}</p>
    <p class="id">Control {{ control.controlId }}</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

{% if crosswalk %}
<h2>Compliance crosswalk</h2>
<p>Where the standard's controls line up with published guidance. Each status
is read straight from the grades above, never claimed beyond them: meets
means every control for that item matches, partially meets means at least one
is present but weaker, misses means a control is absent, and not assessed
means the data could not judge it.</p>
<p><strong>What this is not.</strong> Only the items listed here were mapped.
Each published source contains a great deal this standard does not cover, so
meeting every row below is not the same as meeting the source, and nothing
here is a certification or an audit. Where this standard asks for less than a
source does, the row is left out rather than counted, so a source is never
credited with something the tenant has not actually done.</p>
{% for source in crosswalk %}
<h3>{{ source.source }}</h3>
{% set parts = [] %}
{%- for status in ["meets", "partially meets", "not assessed", "misses"] %}
{%- if source.counts[status] %}{{ parts.append(source.counts[status] ~ " " ~ status) or "" }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
<p class="totals">{{ source.total }} item{{ 's' if source.total != 1 }}: {{ parts | join(", ") }}.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Item</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  {% for row in source.rows[:8] %}
  <tr><td>{{ row.item }}</td><td>{{ row.status }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if source.rows | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ source.rows | length - 8 }} of {{ source.rows | length }} items</summary>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Item</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    {% for row in source.rows[8:] %}
    <tr><td>{{ row.item }}</td><td>{{ row.status }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</details>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if out_of_reach %}
<h2>Not included, because your licensing does not cover it</h2>
<p>These protections are part of the standard but need a licence this tenant
does not have. They are not counted in any grade above, and none of them means
you are doing something wrong. They are listed so the choice is visible: you
can decide whether the protection is worth the licence, rather than never
hearing about it.</p>
<dl class="out-of-reach">
  {% for item in out_of_reach %}
  <dt>{{ item.intent or item.controlId }}</dt>
  <dd>{{ item.note }}{% if item.protects %} What it protects against: {{ item.protects }}{% endif %}
    {% if item.mitigation %}<br>What you can do without the licence: {{ item.mitigation }}
    {% else %}<br>There is no partial alternative recorded for this one, so the
    protection is either licensed or absent.{% endif %}</dd>
  {% endfor %}
</dl>
{% endif %}

<h2>How your setup is organized</h2>
{% if structural %}
<p>These notes are about organization, not security. Nothing here affects any
grade above, and nothing here means you are less protected. The protection is
already in place. They are worth reading only because a tenant that is
organized the same way the standard describes is easier to review later, and
easier to hand to someone else.</p>
<dl class="structural">
  {% for item in structural %}
  <dt>{{ item.intent or item.controlId }}</dt>
  {% for finding in item.findings %}
  <dd>{{ finding }}</dd>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
</dl>
{% else %}
<p>Nothing to note. Where your tenant protects something, it is built the way
the standard describes.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Outside the standard</h2>
{% if surplus %}
<p>These exist in the tenant but are not part of the standard. They are never
penalized in the grades. Review them before any rollout, because a policy
outside the standard can conflict with a planned change.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>State</th></tr>
  {% for item in surplus[:8] %}
  <tr><td>{{ item.displayName }}</td><td>{{ surplus_type_labels.get(item.type, item.type) }}</td><td>{{ item.state }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if surplus | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ surplus | length - 8 }} of {{ surplus | length }} items</summary>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>State</th></tr>
    {% for item in surplus[8:] %}
    <tr><td>{{ item.displayName }}</td><td>{{ surplus_type_labels.get(item.type, item.type) }}</td><td>{{ item.state }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</details>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>Nothing in the tenant sits outside the standard.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>What this assessment cannot see</h2>
<p>An honest list of blind spots. Nothing here was guessed around.</p>
<ul>
{% for item in unknowns[:8] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% if unknowns | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ unknowns | length - 8 }} of {{ unknowns | length }} items</summary>
  <ul>
  {% for item in unknowns[8:] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</details>
{% endif %}

<h2>Tenant context</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Licenses</th>
      <td>{{ context.licenses.skuPartNumbers | join(", ") if context.licenses.skuPartNumbers else "None detected" }}.
      Entra ID P1: {{ "yes" if context.licenses.entraP1 else "no" }}.
      Entra ID P2: {{ "yes" if context.licenses.entraP2 else "no" }}.</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Sign in method registration</th>
      <td class="num">{{ context.registration.mfaRegistered }} of {{ context.registration.totalUsers }} users have registered
      a second sign in factor; {{ context.registration.mfaCapable }} are capable of one.</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Legacy authentication</th>
      <td>{% if context.legacyAuth.eventCount %}{{ context.legacyAuth.eventCount }} sign in event{{ 's' if context.legacyAuth.eventCount != 1 }}
      used older protocols that cannot do modern security checks
      ({{ context.legacyAuth.clients | join(", ") }}).{% else %}No legacy authentication seen in the collection window.{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Global administrators</th>
      <td class="num">{{ context.globalAdministrators.count }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Security defaults</th>
      <td>{{ "Enabled" if context.securityDefaultsEnabled else "Disabled" }}. Security defaults are Microsoft's
      basic protections for tenants without their own policies.</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Federated domains</th>
      <td>{{ context.federatedDomains | join(", ") if context.federatedDomains else "None" }}</td></tr>
</table>

<footer>
<p>{{ scope_note }}</p>
<p>Grades are conservative by design: the report claims protection only when the
collected data proves it.{% if collected_at %} All findings reflect the data collected {{ collected_at }}.{% endif %}
Sign in analysis covers a 30 day window.</p>
<p>To keep a copy, print this page to PDF from the browser.</p>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
